        "style": "transparent",
        "text": "A model emits tokens and nothing else. Given a schema of the calls available to it, it can emit one — a name and arguments — and stop. Your program parses that, does the work, and feeds the result back as more tokens.\n\nHyperLab's assistant works this way, and each action it takes is a Command, which is why you can undo it.",
